        "id": "details",
        "text": "What it shows\nMercury has no sea level. Heights use a reference sphere with a radius of 2,439.4 km; zero means the surface of that sphere.\nReading the scale\nMeters above the reference sphere. Blue is lower and warm colors are higher; values beyond −6,000 or +6,000 m use endpoint colors.\nHow it was made\nUSGS matched surface points across MESSENGER images to build its 2016 global elevation model, version 2.\nLimits\nThe source spacing is about 665 m. The height model was filtered, smoothed and interpolated; this globe displays a coarser sample.\nCoverage\nGray grid marks missing source data."
